{"v":2,"s":"p","w":4,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Acceleration","b":"<p><b>Acceleration</b> (ubrzanje) tells how fast the speed changes:</p><div class=\"fx\">a = Δv / Δt   [m/s²]</div><p>a = 3 m/s² means the speed grows by 3 m/s every second. Braking means negative acceleration.</p><div class=\"callout\">Pressing the gas pedal evenly: the speed grows by the same amount each second.</div>"},{"t":"read","h":"The three formulas","b":"<div class=\"fx\">v = v₀ + a·t</div><div class=\"fx\">s = v₀·t + a·t²/2</div><div class=\"fx\">v² = v₀² + 2·a·s</div><p>Use the third when time isn’t given. From rest, v₀ = 0.</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Graphs","b":"<p>The v–t graph is a sloped line: its slope is a, and the area under it is still the distance. The s–t graph is a parabola.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 144\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Uniformly accelerated motion from rest: v grows in a straight line, and the triangle under it is the distance.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"130\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"20\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"144\" >t</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">v</text><path d=\"M40 130 L250 40 L250 130 Z\" class=\"a2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"40\" class=\"kc\" /><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"130\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"170\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">area = s = at²/2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"11\" class=\"acc\">slope = a</text></svg><figcaption>Uniformly accelerated motion from rest: v grows in a straight line, and the triangle under it is the distance.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A car goes from 0 to 108 km/h in 10 s. Find a and the distance.","s":["108 km/h = 30 m/s.","a = 30/10 = 3 m/s².","s = a·t²/2 = 3 · 100/2 = 150 m."],"a":"a = 3 m/s², s = 150 m"},{"t":"num","q":"From 0 to 20 m/s in 5 s. Acceleration?","a":4,"u":"m/s²","e":"20/5."},{"t":"num","q":"From rest with a = 2 m/s², speed after 3 s?","a":6,"u":"m/s","e":"v = at."},{"t":"num","q":"From rest with a = 3 m/s², distance after 4 s?","a":24,"u":"m","e":"3 · 16/2."},{"t":"num","q":"Braking from 30 m/s with a = −6 m/s². Stopping distance?","a":75,"u":"m","e":"0 = 900 − 12s → s = 75."},{"t":"mc","q":"The area under a v–t graph gives:","o":["acceleration","distance","time","force"],"a":1,"e":"Area = distance, in any motion."}]}